 "positionOnEachFinding": [
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-DEFAULT-PUBLIC-CARRIER",
   "position": "AGREE - reproduced and corrected",
   "rootEvidenceConfirmed": "four distinct (capabilityId, languageMode, workspaceRoot) rows projected to two identical details, because the projection concatenated capabilityId and languageMode into `subject` and DISCARDED workspaceRoot. A doctor report is also a different invocation, and a single StepTermination.domainDetail cannot represent multiple absences.",
   "correction": "New CapabilityAvailabilityNoticeV1 and CapabilityAvailabilityV1 in workflows common, carried on CommandEnvelope.availability - the all-surface parity reference, delivered in the ORIGINAL invocation. The ownership tuple is TYPED (capabilityId, languageMode, workspaceRoot as UserInputPath) and never concatenated, because workspaceRoot is bounded at 4096 while BoundedText is 1024 and a truncated path would collapse two units. A narrow schema extension was taken as authorized rather than forcing reuse.",
   "boundAndCount": "notices maxItems 1024 is EXACTLY the analysis-spec requestedCapabilities bound and an absence exists only for a requested row, so the collection cannot truncate and noticeCount always equals the array length - a stated invariant, not a truncation policy.",
   "verified": "two units, 22 absences, 22 notices, 22 distinct ownership tuples, count equals length, order is the selection order, every notice and the collection admit through the real schemas, and the run envelope carrying the whole collection admits. Candidate-only absences appear per unit and stay advisory: no Coverage, no Control or repair authority, no fabricated Candidate."
  },
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-PUBLIC-ROUTE-COMPLETE",
   "position": "AGREE - reproduced and corrected",
   "rootEvidenceConfirmed": "all three terminations admit, but only the external-config envelope admits; the externally-supplied and host-generated envelopes refuse `errors is a required property`, because those routes leave domainDetail absent and nothing supplied the required array.",
   "correction": "failure_envelope_errors composes the required array: where the termination carries a detail, errors is EXACTLY that detail so the surfaces cannot disagree; where it does not, the route's own envelopeDetail supplies one. Before a Plan or Run exists no run envelope is fabricated. normalize_internal_key matches the LONGEST registered key followed by a colon and carries the remainder as the subject, so real colon-suffixed guard output composes end to end; an unregistered raw string and an impossible origin both refuse.",
   "codesAdded": {
    "count": 4,
    "why": "the failure branch requires a nonempty errors array and these four routes had no code naming their remedy; borrowing an unrelated remedy was refused per root's instruction",
    "codes": [
     "native.capability-spec-invalid",
     "native.release-declaration-invalid",
     "native.coverage-cause-unsupported",
     "HOST.INVARIANT_VIOLATED"
    ],
    "reuseTakenWhereHonest": [
     "external configuration keeps CONFIG.INVALID",
     "a NOT-SELECTED cell keeps PROVIDER.NOT_SELECTED"
    ],
    "registryAndEnumInLockstep": "public-detail-registry 287 records == DomainDetailCode enum 287 members"
   },
   "verified": "all nine real guard outputs compose schema-admitted failure envelopes; four negatives refuse"
  },
  {
   "id": "CX-BV4-PUBLIC-ROUTE-COMPLETE/D9-selected-composition",
   "position": "AGREE - my prose was wrong twice",
   "acceptedCorrections": [
    "Totality was conflated with surjectivity. codeMaps.rule's `total and injective` is a property of the DECLARED CAUSE DOMAIN and does not require every errorCode to have a preimage, so an orphaned error code was never a violation of totality. My claim that the maps were non-total was wrong and is retracted in the source.",
    "`all host-fault events unrepresentable` overstated it. Only the host-INVARIANT subtype was unrepresentable; host-io, ledger-corrupt, provider-protocol and the rest already existed and were always representable.",
    "`no D9 enum change` would be false: faultCause grows by one member. The source now says existing classes, exit codes, reason codes and error codes are unchanged AND that this is a vocabulary extension."
   ],
   "compositionPublishedNow": "native-evidence.schemas.v2.json#/x-opensip-public-route-registry/hostInvariantSuccessor carries the selected normative law in product source rather than deferring it: inherit v1.14 unchanged plus exactly the host-invariant cause mapped to the EXISTING SYSTEM.OUTCOME.ILLEGAL_STATE, with schema, workflow mapper and registry required to agree, every inherited mapping preserved and an unknown cause still refusing. The historical artifact bytes are unchanged.",
   "verified": [
    "the-selected-d9-composition-adds-exactly-one-fault-cause-and-no-code",
    "every-inherited-fault-mapping-is-preserved-exactly",
    "the-declared-cause-domain-stays-total-and-injective",
    "the-prose-does-not-claim-the-inherited-maps-were-nontotal",
    "the-historical-d9-artifact-bytes-are-unchanged"
   ]
  }
 ],
